{"id":"tgw-vs-privatelink-quick-recap","title":"TGW vs PrivateLink (quick recap)"}]},"cards":[{"id":"transit-001","type":"concept","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"VPC peering: how many VPCs does one connection join, and is it transitive?","back":{"answer":"Exactly two VPCs (1:1), and it is non-transitive.","explanation":"If A peers B and B peers C, A still cannot reach C. Every pair needs its own peering.","mnemonic":"Peering = a 1:1 cable between two buildings.","code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":1,"tags":["vpc-peering","transitive"],"sourceHeading":"The idea","examTip":"non-transitive"},
{"id":"transit-002","type":"fact","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"How many peering connections does full connectivity between n VPCs need? Example for 10 VPCs?","back":{"answer":"n(n-1)/2; 10 VPCs = 45 peerings (25 VPCs = 300).","explanation":"Adding on-premises links makes the mesh unmanageable.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":2,"tags":["vpc-peering","mesh"],"sourceHeading":"The idea","examTip":"n(n-1)/2"},
{"id":"transit-003","type":"concept","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"What is AWS Transit Gateway (TGW) and what topology does it give?","back":{"answer":"A central hub; each VPC, VPN or Direct Connect gets one attachment — star topology with transitive routing.","explanation":"A can reach C through the hub with no direct cable.","mnemonic":"TGW is the airport hub.","code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":1,"tags":["transit-gateway","hub-and-spoke"],"sourceHeading":"The idea","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-004","type":"fact","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"Transit Gateway: how are VPCs attached?","back":{"answer":"Thousands of VPCs, one attachment each.","explanation":null,"mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":1,"tags":["transit-gateway","vpc"],"sourceHeading":"What you can attach","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-005","type":"fact","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"Transit Gateway: how does on-premises connect via Site-to-Site VPN?","back":{"answer":"A Site-to-Site VPN attachment connects on-prem over the internet.","explanation":null,"mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":1,"tags":["transit-gateway","vpn"],"sourceHeading":"What you can attach","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-006","type":"fact","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"Transit Gateway: how does Direct Connect attach?","back":{"answer":"Via a transit VIF.","explanation":null,"mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":1,"tags":["transit-gateway","direct-connect"],"sourceHeading":"What you can attach","examTip":"transit VIF"},
{"id":"transit-007","type":"fact","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"Transit Gateway: how do you connect TGWs across regions?","back":{"answer":"Attach another TGW using TGW peering.","explanation":null,"mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":1,"tags":["transit-gateway","tgw-peering"],"sourceHeading":"What you can attach","examTip":"TGW peering"},
{"id":"transit-008","type":"concept","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"How do you share a Transit Gateway across AWS accounts?","back":{"answer":"Share it with AWS RAM (Resource Access Manager).","explanation":"One hub for the whole organization.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":1,"tags":["transit-gateway","ram"],"sourceHeading":"What you can attach","examTip":"RAM"},
{"id":"transit-009","type":"concept","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"How does Transit Gateway isolate prod from dev while both use the same hub?","back":{"answer":"Use separate TGW route tables per attachment (segmentation).","explanation":"Prod can't see dev, yet both can still route to on-premises.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":2,"tags":["transit-gateway","route-tables","segmentation"],"sourceHeading":"What you can attach","examTip":"route tables"},
{"id":"transit-010","type":"trap","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"Which AWS service is the ONLY one supporting IP multicast?","back":{"answer":"Transit Gateway.","explanation":"See the word \"multicast\" and the answer is Transit Gateway.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":1,"tags":["transit-gateway","multicast"],"sourceHeading":"What you can attach","examTip":"multicast"},
{"id":"transit-011","type":"concept","subtopic":"what-you-can-attach","front":"What does Transit Gateway appliance mode do?","back":{"answer":"Keeps both directions of a flow going through the same network appliance (firewall/inspection VPC).","explanation":"The keyword for centralized traffic inspection.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":2,"tags":["transit-gateway","appliance-mode"],"sourceHeading":"What you can attach","examTip":"appliance mode"},
{"id":"transit-012","type":"compare","subtopic":"cost-reality-check","front":"Transit Gateway vs VPC peering: how is each charged?","back":{"answer":"TGW: per attachment per hour plus per GB processed. Peering: no hourly charge, just data transfer.","explanation":null,"mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":2,"tags":["transit-gateway","vpc-peering","cost"],"sourceHeading":"Cost reality check","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-013","type":"compare","subtopic":"cost-reality-check","front":"When is VPC peering still the right choice over Transit Gateway?","back":{"answer":"When only 2–3 VPCs need to talk: cheaper and simpler.","explanation":"TGW earns its keep with many VPCs, on-prem connectivity and transitive routing.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":2,"tags":["vpc-peering","transit-gateway","cost"],"sourceHeading":"Cost reality check","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-014","type":"compare","subtopic":"tgw-vs-privatelink-quick-recap","front":"Transit Gateway/peering vs PrivateLink: how do they differ?","back":{"answer":"TGW/peering join whole networks; PrivateLink exposes only one service through an endpoint.","explanation":"Overlapping CIDRs are fine with PrivateLink.","mnemonic":"Network marriage vs service window.","code":null},"choices":null,"difficulty":2,"tags":["transit-gateway","privatelink"],"sourceHeading":"TGW vs PrivateLink (quick recap)","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-015","type":"scenario","subtopic":"patterns","front":"25 VPCs and an on-premises datacenter need centralized connectivity. Which solution?","back":{"answer":"Transit Gateway.","explanation":"Hub-and-spoke removes the n(n-1)/2 mesh.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":[{"text":"VPC peering mesh","correct":false,"why":"Needs 300 peerings; unmanageable."},{"text":"Transit Gateway","correct":true,"why":"Hub-and-spoke replaces the mesh."},{"text":"PrivateLink","correct":false,"why":"Exposes one service, not networks."},{"text":"Internet gateway","correct":false,"why":"Public path, not private hub."}],"difficulty":3,"tags":["transit-gateway"],"sourceHeading":"Question patterns","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-016","type":"scenario","subtopic":"patterns","front":"VPC A peers with B, B peers with C, but A can't reach C. What fixes this?","back":{"answer":"Transit Gateway.","explanation":"Peering is non-transitive; TGW routes transitively.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":[{"text":"Edit security groups","correct":false,"why":"Problem is routing, not filtering."},{"text":"Larger instance types","correct":false,"why":"Irrelevant to routing."},{"text":"Transit Gateway","correct":true,"why":"Provides transitive routing."},{"text":"Elastic IPs","correct":false,"why":"Doesn't create transitive routes."}],"difficulty":3,"tags":["transit-gateway","transitive"],"sourceHeading":"Question patterns","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-017","type":"scenario","subtopic":"patterns","front":"Prod VPCs must not talk to dev VPCs, but all need on-prem access. Design?","back":{"answer":"TGW with separate route tables per attachment.","explanation":"Segmentation at the hub.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":[{"text":"VPC peering between all","correct":false,"why":"Doesn't isolate; mesh complexity."},{"text":"Single shared TGW route table","correct":false,"why":"Prod and dev would see each other."},{"text":"PrivateLink for each VPC","correct":false,"why":"Not for full network access."},{"text":"TGW with separate route tables","correct":true,"why":"Segments prod and dev at the hub."}],"difficulty":3,"tags":["transit-gateway","segmentation"],"sourceHeading":"Question patterns","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-018","type":"scenario","subtopic":"patterns","front":"An application requires IP multicast. Which AWS service?","back":{"answer":"Transit Gateway.","explanation":"The only service that supports it.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":[{"text":"VPC peering","correct":false,"why":"No multicast support."},{"text":"Transit Gateway","correct":true,"why":"Only service supporting multicast."},{"text":"PrivateLink","correct":false,"why":"No multicast support."},{"text":"Direct Connect","correct":false,"why":"Not a multicast service."}],"difficulty":3,"tags":["transit-gateway","multicast"],"sourceHeading":"Question patterns","examTip":"multicast"},
{"id":"transit-019","type":"scenario","subtopic":"patterns","front":"Just 2 VPCs need to communicate at lowest cost. Which?","back":{"answer":"VPC peering.","explanation":"No hourly charge; TGW would be overkill.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":[{"text":"Transit Gateway","correct":false,"why":"Hourly attachment fees; overkill."},{"text":"Site-to-Site VPN","correct":false,"why":"Adds cost and complexity."},{"text":"VPC peering","correct":true,"why":"No hourly charge for two VPCs."},{"text":"PrivateLink","correct":false,"why":"Exposes services, has hourly cost."}],"difficulty":3,"tags":["vpc-peering","cost"],"sourceHeading":"Question patterns","examTip":null},
{"id":"transit-020","type":"scenario","subtopic":"patterns","front":"Share the network hub across 50 AWS accounts. How?","back":{"answer":"TGW shared via AWS RAM.","explanation":null,"mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":[{"text":"Peer every account's VPC","correct":false,"why":"Mesh explosion."},{"text":"Copy TGW to each account","correct":false,"why":"TGW is shared, not copied."},{"text":"IAM role per account","correct":false,"why":"IAM doesn't share the hub."},{"text":"Share TGW via AWS RAM","correct":true,"why":"RAM shares the hub across accounts."}],"difficulty":3,"tags":["transit-gateway","ram"],"sourceHeading":"Question patterns","examTip":"RAM"},
{"id":"transit-021","type":"scenario","subtopic":"patterns","front":"Connect hub networks in us-east-1 and eu-west-1. What?","back":{"answer":"TGW peering.","explanation":"Cross-region hub-to-hub.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":[{"text":"TGW peering","correct":true,"why":"Connects TGW hubs across regions."},{"text":"Route 53","correct":false,"why":"DNS only, no connectivity."},{"text":"Internet gateway","correct":false,"why":"Public, not hub-to-hub."},{"text":"PrivateLink","correct":false,"why":"Single service exposure."}],"difficulty":3,"tags":["transit-gateway","tgw-peering"],"sourceHeading":"Question patterns","examTip":"TGW peering"},
{"id":"transit-022","type":"scenario","subtopic":"patterns","front":"All inter-VPC traffic must pass through a firewall appliance. Solution?","back":{"answer":"TGW with appliance mode.","explanation":"Symmetric flows through the inspection VPC.","mnemonic":null,"code":null},"choices":[{"text":"VPC peering with NACLs","correct":false,"why":"No symmetric appliance routing."},{"text":"PrivateLink","correct":false,"why":"Not for inter-VPC inspection."},{"text":"Route 53 Resolver","correct":false,"why":"DNS only."},{"text":"TGW with appliance mode","correct":true,"why":"Keeps both flow directions on one appliance."}],"difficulty":3,"tags":["transit-gateway","appliance-mode"],"sourceHeading":"Question patterns","examTip":"appliance mode"},
